## Summary

Shipped `apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/FleetStatsWidget.*` (8 files, 1,483 LOC) at parity with `web/.../FleetStatsWidget.tsx` (+ `FleetStatsBar`), following the established `0064 MileageStatsWidget` parallel-surface pattern.

**What it does** — five fleet metric tiles in an adaptive grid (Fleet Size + online count · 30-day Distance + sparkline · 30-day Energy + sparkline · Efficiency · Alerts), a title-less glass shell with freshness chip + refresh, and all six states (loading/empty/error/stale/offline/content).

**Architecture** — P1/S8 state-holder seam (`FleetStatsSource`→`FleetStatsModel`, no HTTP in the view) · P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry (`surface: FleetStatsWidget`) · P1/S10 i18n facade (all 8 source keys `fleet.*` + chrome) · P1/S9 design tokens (no neon/raw hex) · registry `fleet-stats` (analytics, 4×2/2×2/4×40). The web `MiniChart` SVG polyline is ported 1:1 as a SwiftUI `Path` (`FleetSparkline`); the web's `total_distance_km`→SI-converter quirk is reproduced verbatim (no silent unit "fix"). Consumes (doesn't redefine) the shared grid primitives.

